# External (game-rip) asset packs + their share bundle — NEVER commit: no
# redistribution licence + multi-GB binaries. Transferred privately via
# tools/pack_external_assets.ps1 -> tools/unpack_external_assets.ps1.
acc_external_assets.zip

# Perk-shader folder is MIXED (2026-07-10 split): the hand-written GDT + our own
# July-2026 HUD art (badges, OC/PaP tiers, data shard, blank) ARE committed; only
# the Ronan-derived rip art (Apr-2023 files + hexshield backups) stays out and
# rides the private external-assets zip (manifest entry "Perk-icon shaders").
# NEVER re-add a wholesale dir ignore here — it silently untracked our badges.
source_data/acc_perk_shaders/_images/acc_perk_*.png
source_data/acc_perk_shaders/_images/i_acc_perk_*.png
source_data/acc_perk_shaders/_images/i_acc_powerup_*.png
source_data/acc_perk_shaders/_images/i_acc_pap_tier*.png.acc-hexshield-orig
source_data/acc_perk_shaders/_images/i_acc_data_shard.png.acc-128-orig

# Audio source WAVs: our CC0 audio (sound_assets/acc/**) IS committed (Workshop-
# safe, 48k/16-bit). The game-rip weapon/boss ports live ONLY in the Mod Tools tree
# (installed via the external-asset unpack flow) — never commit them if they appear
# under sound_assets/ here.
/sound_assets/skye_ports/
/sound_assets/_NSZ/

# COPYRIGHTED test-only music — DO NOT COMMIT and DO NOT SHIP PUBLIC (CREDITS.md IP
# gate). "115" = Treyarch/Kevin Sherwood; paradise_calm = Nintendo Mario "Stage Win";
# ee_song_3 = Rosa Walton "I Really Want to Stay at Your House" (Cyberpunk: Edgerunners
# / CD PROJEKT RED). Placeholder test tracks; swap for CC0 before any Public Workshop
# release. All three ride the manifest "Copyrighted placeholder music" private-zip entry.
# (ee_song_3.wav was accidentally committed in 90aa25b — untracked 2026-07-10; the blob
# still lives in that commit's history, scrub separately if the GitHub repo is public.)
/sound_assets/acc/music/115.wav
/sound_assets/acc/music/paradise_calm.wav
/sound_assets/acc/music/ee_song_3.wav

